    "verdict": "KBC gradual decay NOT observed: H0 changes from 72.3 at z < 0.15 to 73.5 at z > 0.25 (\u0394 = +1.2 km/s/Mpc). The published KBC/MOND model (HBK20/Mazurenko et al. 2024) predicts a gradual decline towards the Planck value (67.4), but the observed H0 does not decline \u2014 it is flat or increases. NOTE: The absolute H0 = 73.5 at z > 0.25 is NOT an independent measurement; Pantheon+ MU_SH0ES uses M_B = -19.253 calibrated from Cepheid anchors, so the Cepheid zero-point is inherited by construction. The calibration-independent test is the relative evolution, which rejects the KBC gradual decline. The TEP prediction (flat H0(z) for global M_B) is consistent with the observed flat profile. The host-mass dependence of the TEP effect is established in TEP-H0 (Paper 11) using per-host Cepheid distances, not the global M_B used here."
